 "root": "root",
 "note": "Machine-traversable index of all public work. Cognitive state is a first-class field: `survived` has passed a real test, `speculative` is untested theory, `retired` was killed by its own falsification and is kept as a tombstone. Covers published research only; private notes and correspondence are not indexed.",
 "languageNote": "One graph carries both languages; there is no second Chinese graph, because a second graph is a second thing to rot. `label` and `description` are language-tagged maps (JSON-LD @container: @language) and may be partial -- an English-only label means no Chinese title has been written, not that one is missing by error. `inLanguage` states what language the ARTIFACT is written in, which is not the language of the index pointing at it -- four of the research pages are Chinese-only while llms.txt is English. Where a work exists in both languages, the node carries the English canonical in `url` and points at its Chinese edition with `workTranslation`; the pairing is also visible in the filename, which takes a `.zh.` infix. Two of the three theory notes were written in Chinese first and translated afterwards, so their Chinese editions are originals rather than derivatives -- `workTranslation` records which URL is canonical for agents, not which text came first. `cognitiveState` and `confidence` are deliberately single-valued and untranslated: the epistemic layer is not a property of a language. A claim retired in English is retired in Chinese.",
 "schemaNote": "v1 breaks v0 consumers that expected `label`/`description` to be plain strings; they are now language maps. v0 also silently renamed the vocabulary it claimed to extend. The mapping is now stated explicitly in `stateVocabulary` instead of being folklore.",
 "stateVocabulary": {
  "values": [
   "survived",
   "speculative",
   "retired"
  ],
  "closed": true,
  "mapsFrom": {
   "note": "This site index `extends` cognition-track/manifest/v0, whose vocabulary is NOT the same. The rename was undocumented until now. This is the mapping, and it is the only sanctioned one -- a third variant must not appear.",
   "survived-stress-test": "survived",
   "speculative": "speculative",
   "raw": "(not used here; this index publishes nothing in a raw state)",
   "retired": "(no counterpart in cognition-track/manifest/v0, which expresses retirement with a `falsifies` edge instead of a state. This index does BOTH: a retired node carries the state AND the falsifies edge.)"
  }
 },
