  {
   "id": "learning-the-self-boundary-log",
   "label": {
    "en": "Stage log - the self-boundary line, in order",
    "zh": "阶段日志 - 自我边界这条线,按顺序"
   },
   "description": {
    "en": "The audit trail for the self-boundary note: one row per stage (specification, prior-art audit, evidence audits, three rounds of data hunting, two human re-analyses, three simulation stages), each stating what it overturned or established. Mostly a record of self-inflicted damage, including three reusable mistakes: reading a probe's signal-to-noise as the system's coupling strength and then shipping that misdiagnosis downstream as a premise; believing three separate trial-level-data-available statements that all turned out to be aggregates with no trial index; and letting an unreferenced claim of empirical establishment carry an architectural conclusion.",
    "zh": "自我边界那篇的审计留痕:每个阶段一行(规格、prior-art 审计、证据审计、三轮数据搜寻、两次人类数据重分析、三个仿真阶段),各自说明它推翻或确立了什么。主要是一份自伤记录,含三条可复用的错误:把探针的信噪比读成系统的耦合强度并把误诊当前提发给下一棒;连着相信三份「逐试次数据公开」的声明,打开全是没有试次序号的聚合表;以及让一句无出处的「经验上确凿」承载了一整条架构结论。"
   },
   "url": "https://machengshen.github.io/theory/learning-the-self-boundary-log.md",
   "format": "text/markdown",
   "inLanguage": "en",
   "workTranslation": "https://machengshen.github.io/theory/learning-the-self-boundary-log.zh.md",
   "cognitiveState": "speculative",
   "confidence": 0.15,
   "edges": [
    {
     "relation": "supports",
     "target": "learning-the-self-boundary"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "no-state-only-history",
   "label": {
    "en": "No state, only history",
    "zh": "没有 state,只有 history"
   },
   "description": {
    "en": "A corrected diagnosis of vanilla Transformer inference. It has activation state, computational state and a transient workspace-like representational state; Anthropic's J-space gives causal evidence for the last. The narrower missing object is a persistent autonomous path-dependent closure state that maintains its own projection and forgetting policy across steps. E1 still establishes that Grassmann subspace change is not a monotone function of update magnitude. The earlier claim that thresholding this gate implies bistability is withdrawn: E3 now requires carrier-matched controls, two stable branches and remanence, and its mechanism confidence is reset to 0.35.",
    "zh": "对 vanilla Transformer inference 的修正诊断:它有 activation state、computational state 与瞬时 workspace-like representational state;Anthropic J-space 为最后一项提供了因果证据。真正缺失的对象收窄为跨步持续、具有路径依赖并自主维护自身投影与遗忘策略的 closure state。E1 仍证明 Grassmann 子空间变化不是更新幅度的单调函数。此前“阈值化门控推出双稳态”的说法撤回:E3 现在要求 carrier-matched controls、两条稳定分支与 remanence,机制置信度重置为 0.35。"
   },
   "url": "https://machengshen.github.io/theory/no-state-only-history.md",
   "format": "text/markdown",
   "inLanguage": "en",
   "cognitiveState": "speculative",
   "confidence": 0.3
  },
  {
   "id": "consciousness-as-quantum-mechanics",
   "label": {
    "en": "Can consciousness be studied mathematically, the way quantum mechanics is?",
    "zh": "能不能像研究量子力学那样,用数学研究意识?"
   },
   "description": {
    "en": "A boundary note amended in 2026. High-dimensional states and joint variables are legitimate modelling choices but have no quantum specificity; classical coupling already covers the relationship examples. The earlier equivalence among non-exact forms, holonomy, path dependence, hysteresis, memory and consciousness is withdrawn. Unitary dynamics can encode history, so the real missing ingredients are an empirically identified generator, environment and coarse-graining protocol. J-space, COGITATE and anaesthetized-hippocampus evidence are used to separate reportability, complex representation, plasticity and consciousness.",
    "zh": "一篇于 2026 年修订的边界笔记。高维状态与联合变量是合法模型选择,但没有量子专属性;经典耦合已覆盖文中关系例子。此前把非恰当形式、holonomy、路径依赖、滞回、记忆与意识等同的说法撤回。幺正动力学可以编码历史,真正缺失的是实验识别出的生成元、环境与粗粒化协议。J-space、COGITATE 与麻醉海马证据被用于拆开可报告性、复杂表征、可塑性与意识。"
   },
   "url": "https://machengshen.github.io/theory/consciousness-as-quantum-mechanics.md",
   "format": "text/markdown",
   "inLanguage": "zh-Hans",
   "cognitiveState": "speculative",
   "confidence": 0.25
  },
  {
   "id": "information-and-qi",
   "label": {
    "en": "Information and qi — a comparison note on a parallel line",
    "zh": "信息与气 —— 对一条平行线路的对照笔记"
   },
   "description": {
    "en": "Addressed to the YouTube channel @itsRedPill and its readers; compares a line arrived at independently from reinforcement learning, decision theory and robotics against that channel's information-ontology arcs. Framed by its author as an invitation rather than a scorecard. Five parts: four points of verbatim convergence (we touch only models; the real-versus-simulated dichotomy does not hold; the self is a process; and, flagged as most valuable, embodiment plus a requirement to maintain one's own existence); the step deliberately declined (the qi slot, dissolved rather than answered, since if the true state of the world is ill-posed so is the question of what underlies the projection); three places judged not to hold up, each with named literature and a stated way to settle it; a constructive replacement for one; and three suggestions. Applies its anti-grand-unification rule symmetrically and states the cost of its own branch. Claims tagged by honesty level. The author states the cognitive state as exploratory and non-conclusive in the text.",
    "zh": "写给 YouTube 频道 @itsRedPill 及其读者的对照笔记,把一条从强化学习/决策论/机器人学独立走出的线与该频道的信息本体论系列对照,作者定性为邀请而非评分卡。五段:四处共识;一步主动不走的(气那个槽位,取消问题而非回答);三处判断站不住脚处,各附文献与判决方式;其中一处的建设性替代;三条建议。对自己用同一把尺子,并列出自己这条路的代价。论断按诚实度标注。作者正文自述认知状态为探索性、非结论。"
   },
   "url": "https://machengshen.github.io/information-and-qi.html",
   "format": "text/html",
   "inLanguage": "zh-Hans",
