   "id": "agent-safety-stewardship",
   "label": {
    "en": "Agent safety as anti-cancer governance",
    "zh": "Agent 安全：一种防癌变治理"
   },
   "description": {
    "en": "A control-theoretic account of cancer-like persistent-agent failure: local survival, repair, and replication decoupled from owner-level purpose, bounded authority, stop inheritance, resource budgets, and independent verification. Defines seven runtime invariants and an A–D disclosure rule: never publish the growth engine separated from its immune system.",
    "zh": "把常驻 Agent 的癌变式失控理解为一种控制病理：局部生存、修复和复制脱离 owner 层目的、有界权限、stop 继承、资源预算和独立验证。给出七条运行时不变量与 A–D 分层披露规则：永远不要把增长引擎从免疫系统上拆下来单独发布。"
   },
